Z||000000||jhar1987||04-27-2001||04:55 PM||||not really but still need your help! it died going to work this morning and won't refire. last nite i put a new oil pressure switch and fuel pump relay, drove the car alover for two hours with no problem, this morning got half mile down the road and she quit. what should i check next? the fuel pump is working as of 5 min. ago. thanks jeff||||reg||1
Z||000001||jaguiler||04-27-2001||05:03 PM||||Chk your fuel pump fuse first..... I screwed around in my engine one day.... took off the decklid and unplugged the plug that goes to that.....<BR>I went to start the car...and nothing.....  I did not hear the pump go (do you hear yours?) so I chked the fuses.... you should have a functional fuel pump fuse.....<BR>sorry if this advice seems kind of basic...but you never know....<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||04-27-2001||06:18 PM||||I still recommend checking the fuel pump itself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jhar1987||04-27-2001||07:12 PM||||ed even if i can hear it come on there still can be a prob? to update 2 hrs ago she wouldn't start as of an hour ago,without doing anything she fired and has been running for 45min. as you can imagine i am not quick to test drive since i have towed it home three times this week.thanks jeff||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-27-2001||07:20 PM||||Exactly what has been replaced so far???<P><BR>check all the battery connections. especially the thin ones.<P>check the big terminal block(C500) next to the battery. take out the locking bolt. seperate it. clean it. repack it with "dielectric grease" and reassemble it. You can get the terminal grease at any parts store or electronics shop.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||04-27-2001||10:07 PM||||The ignition module will act like this. when it gets hot or warm it quits then when it cools down it will fire up. About the only way you can check these is just replace it, they are not that expensive, and no trouble to put in. I am talking about the V-6.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fyerstarter||04-27-2001||10:19 PM||||you can take the module to autozone and get it tested.<P>you may want to do the ol check for spark and fuel before you do.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||04-27-2001||10:36 PM||||Modules that test good at the store may not work in Fiero.<P>A big problem is heat. Read my heat management articles for a better idea why.<P>A store tester rarely runs a module under the same conditions a Fiero will. V6 is the worst because of where the distributor is, but 84-86 4 cylinder aren't much better.||||reg||1
Z||000008||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-27-2001||10:57 PM||||old ignition module connot be trusted<P>always listen to the ogre . . .||||reg||1
